    "abstract": "LoRA freezes pretrained Transformer weights and injects trainable rank-decomposition matrices into selected layers, so a weight update is represented as BA with small rank r. It reduces trainable parameters by up to 10,000x and GPU memory by about 3x for GPT-3 175B while matching or exceeding full fine-tuning quality, and adds no inference latency because BA can be merged into W0.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "A weight update can be parameterised as Delta W = B A with rank r << min(d, k) while W0 stays frozen.",
      "On GPT-3 175B, LoRA reduces trainable parameters by about 10,000x and GPU memory by about 3x relative to full fine-tuning.",
      "LoRA matches or exceeds fine-tuning quality on RoBERTa, DeBERTa, GPT-2 and GPT-3 benchmarks.",
      "Because BA can be merged into W0, LoRA introduces no additional inference latency.",
      "A very small rank (even r=1 or 2) adapting W_q and W_v is often sufficient."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
    "arxivist_version": "1.0"
